  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the App Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the app\'s structural elements. Building this launcher needs a layered architecture, moving away from standard reliance on generic solutions. The aim is to create a custom, accessible launcher ideal for elderly users or those with motor disabilities, and the structure has to reflect that.\n\n\n**Analyzing UI Interaction**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the UI interaction, especially concerning voice commands. The integration of Gemini NLU as an orchestration engine seems promising. I\'m focusing on how intent translates into native Android API execution, considering the visual cues and button interactions in this context. The UI design, with large tiles and voice commands, looks appropriate for the target users.\n\n\n**Refining Button Designs**\n\nI\'m now refining the button designs, considering color-coding and visual cues for intuitive interaction. I\'m focusing on making the pill buttons distinct with colored borders, accentuating their function. The bottom button, featuring the microphone icon, will have a clear prompt for voice interaction.\n\n\n**Defining Core Actions**\n\nI\'m now defining the core actions for the app, including making calls, opening apps, and reading notifications. The contacts resolver uses `ContactsContract` with fuzzy matching for a streamlined lookup. Voice input integrates seamlessly with Gemini NLU, offering both feedback and TTS. I\'m ensuring full UI match to design mockups, with switchable grid and list layouts, high-contrast elements, and big touch targets for easy interaction.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 274126097
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
