  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Voice Input**\n\nI\'m working on a microphone-enabled UI component for Jetpack Compose, considering its place within the Accessible Voice Launcher app. The initial design prioritizes seamless permission handling, so this critical piece will work consistently and reliably. We\'re aiming for immediate integration with the app.\n\n\n**Refining Implementation Strategy**\n\nI\'ve decided to leverage `rememberLauncherForActivityResult` for permission handling, steering away from the deprecated Accompanist Permissions. This simplified approach streamlines the dependency profile and the overall code complexity, making it easier to integrate the new component. Next step: the UI!\n\n\n**Prioritizing Zero-Dependency**\n\nI\'ve opted to stick with `ActivityResultContracts` for audio permission handling, eliminating the need for the Accompanist Permissions library. This minimizes dependencies and keeps the code streamlined. Moving forward, I\'m focusing on the component\'s core functionality, deciding between a `SpeechRecognizer` and a `RecognizerIntent` implementation, while also keeping in mind the target user group. My current preference leans towards the in-app `SpeechRecognizer`.\n\n\n**Implementing Speech Recognition**\n\nI\'m now starting to implement the `VoiceInputComponent.kt` file. A standard `SpeechRecognizer` approach seems best; I\'ll implement `RecognitionListener`. It will involve running on the main thread. I\'m focusing on that right now to make it work.\n\n\n**Constructing Voice Input Button**\n\nI\'m now building the `VoiceInputButton` composable function and integrating the permission check and launcher directly.  I\'m using `rememberLauncherForActivityResult` for audio permission. Next, I\'ll integrate `mutableStateOf` to manage the listening state, and I\'ll include error handling for the permission. I\'m focusing on the component\'s structure and state management.\n\n\n**Handling Speech Recognition Errors**\n\nI\'m now integrating error handling for speech recognition. I\'ve included a `RecognitionListener` to catch and manage potential issues.  I\'m handling error cases like audio recording problems and insufficient permissions to ensure the `VoiceInputButton` responds appropriately. I\'m focusing on providing informative feedback to the user when things go wrong, and updating the state of the component accordingly.\n\n\n**Refining Error Feedback**\n\nI\'m currently working to improve error messaging. I\'ve implemented detailed error handling in the `RecognitionListener` to provide specific feedback. I\'m taking care to show users exactly what went wrong when things don\'t go as expected. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness when managing error conditions. I also have the `onResult` functionality implemented.\n\n\n**Finalizing Audio Capture**\n\nI\'m now integrating `DisposableEffect` to properly manage and destroy the `speechRecognizer`, ensuring we clean up resources. I\'ve built in `startListening()` and `stopListening()` to manage the speech process, as well as an intent and `startListening()` to initiate speech capture. My focus is finalizing this audio capture process.\n\n\n**Integrating UI Updates**\n\nI\'m now integrating the UI with the core functionality. I\'ve focused on updating the button\'s appearance based on its state, like the \"Listening...\" text. The semantics are in, making sure the button is accessible. I\'m prioritizing user feedback, so the button makes it clear whether or not it is listening.\n\n\n**Integrating Voice Input**\n\nI\'m now integrating the voice input component into the application\'s structure. I\'ll create the `VoiceInputComponent.kt` file, and I\'ll carefully check `AndroidManifest.xml` to ensure the audio recording permission is correctly declared, referencing the previous PDF context. This will make it seamless to integrate voice input to match the user\'s specific request.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 15
      nanos: 121411598
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
