cer` occupies the space. I\'m also preparing for an accessible grid layout using a `Column` and `Row` structure, and I\'ll include boxes within for component organization. The layout will include spacing and alignment.\n\n\n**Adding Accessible Buttons**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating accessible buttons for enhanced user interaction. I\'m adding a phone icon button and an \"SOS\" button within a `Row` layout. I\'m using specific background colors and setting up click actions. The buttons will now occupy equal space using a `Box` with `Modifier.weight`.\n\n\n**Adding More Accessible Buttons**\n\nI\'m now expanding the accessible button functionality. I\'m adding two more buttons within the existing layout, to create a row with the others. I\'m adding a chat icon button, and a person icon button, using two separate boxes for organization, with green and blue backgrounds respectively. I\'m setting the `weight` modifier to ensure they occupy equal space, with the same alignment.\n\n\n**Defining the Custom Button**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `AccessibleButton` composable function. It handles both icon and text buttons, using a `Box` for centering and styling. The button is defined to have a circular shape and white border. I\'ve integrated click functionality and background color customization. The function will accept `ImageVector?` for icons or a `String?` for text.\n\n\n**Adding the Bottom Navigation**\n\nI\'m now integrating the bottom navigation bar. I\'ve designed a `Row` layout, using the color scheme `Color(0xFF222226)`. I\'ve added icons for Home and Undo, along with click functionality for the manual voice trigger and text, with customized sizes and colors.\n\n\n"
