steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1788836655
      nanos: 101010096
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Prepare this completed Google AI Studio Android app for automatic debug APK building and\nGitHub Release publishing with GitHub Actions.\nBefore creating anything, confirm that:\ngradle/libs.versions.toml\ncontains exactly:\nagp = \"9.1.1\"\nIf the AGP version is not exactly 9.1.1:\n\342\227\217   Stop immediately.\n\342\227\217   Report the detected AGP value.\n\342\227\217   Do not create the workflow.\n\342\227\217   Do not modify any file.\nIf the AGP version is exactly 9.1.1, create only:\n.github/workflows/build-apk.yml\nDo not create, edit, delete, rename, format, upgrade, or replace any other repository file.\n\nDo not modify the Android app, source code, design, features, package name, application ID,\nmanifest, resources, dependencies, Gradle project files, signing configuration, or project\nsettings.\nThe workflow must build the debug APK, preserve it as a normal GitHub Actions artifact, and\npublish the same APK directly under GitHub Releases for easy downloading on a phone.\nWorkflow triggers\nCreate a GitHub Actions workflow that:\n\342\227\217   Runs automatically on every push to the main branch.\n\342\227\217   Also supports workflow_dispatch.\n\342\227\217   Does not run on pull requests.\n\342\227\217   Uses ubuntu-latest.\n\342\227\217   Checks out the complete repository.\n\342\227\217   Runs all Gradle commands from the repository root.\nWorkflow permissions\nAdd only the permission required to create a GitHub Release:\npermissions:\ncontents: write\nDo not request unnecessary permissions.\nDo not use a personal access token, repository secret, external API key, deployment key, or\ncustom credential.\nUse only the workflow\'s built-in GitHub token for release creation:\n${{ github.token }}\nJava setup\nSet up Temurin Java 17 using actions/setup-java.\nJava must be configured before Gradle is configured or any Gradle command is executed.\nAdd a step named:\nVerify Java environment\n\nThat step must:\n\342\227\217   Run java -version.\n\342\227\217   Print JAVA_HOME.\n\342\227\217   Detect the active Java major version.\n\342\227\217   Confirm that the active Java major version is 17 or newer.\n\342\227\217   Fail clearly if Java is lower than 17.\n\342\227\217   Fail clearly if the Java version cannot be detected.\nGradle setup\nSet up exactly Gradle 9.3.1 using gradle/actions/setup-gradle.\nDo not use:\n\342\227\217   Gradle 8.13\n\342\227\217   The repository Gradle wrapper\n\342\227\217   latest\n\342\227\217   current\n\342\227\217   release-candidate\n\342\227\217   nightly\n\342\227\217   Any Gradle version other than exactly 9.3.1\nRun all Gradle commands from the repository root.\nTemporary debug keystore\nBefore building, add a step named:\nCreate temporary debug keystore\nThat step must:\n\342\227\217   Check whether ./debug.keystore already exists.\n\342\227\217   Generate it only when it is missing.\n\342\227\217   Use keytool from the configured Java 17 installation.\n\342\227\217   Use exactly:\n\342\227\213   Keystore password: android\n\342\227\213   Key alias: androiddebugkey\n\342\227\213   Key password: android\n\342\227\213   Distinguished name: CN=Android Debug,O=Android,C=US\n\342\227\213   Algorithm: RSA\n\342\227\213   Key size: 2048\n\342\227\213   Validity: 10000 days\n\n\342\227\217   Confirm that ./debug.keystore exists after generation.\n\342\227\217   Fail clearly if the keystore cannot be created.\n\342\227\217   Never commit the keystore.\n\342\227\217   Never cache the keystore.\n\342\227\217   Never print the keystore.\n\342\227\217   Never expose the keystore.\n\342\227\217   Never preserve the keystore after the workflow runner is removed.\n\342\227\217   Never upload the keystore as an artifact or release asset.\nBuild the debug APK\nBuild the debug APK using exactly:\ngradle :app:assembleDebug --stacktrace --no-daemon\nDo not replace this command with:\n\342\227\217   ./gradlew\n\342\227\217   gradlew\n\342\227\217   assembleRelease\n\342\227\217   bundleRelease\n\342\227\217   assemble\n\342\227\217   build\n\342\227\217   Any other Gradle command\nVerify the APK\nAfter the build, verify that this exact file exists:\napp/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\nIf the exact file is missing:\n\342\227\217   Search only inside app/build/outputs/apk.\n\342\227\217   Print the APK paths discovered inside that directory.\n\342\227\217   Do not search the entire repository.\n\342\227\217   Do not select a release APK.\n\342\227\217   Do not select an Android test APK.\n\342\227\217   Do not select an APK from another module.\n\342\227\217   Do not upload or release an unrelated APK.\n\342\227\217   Fail clearly if the expected debug APK does not exist.\nConfirm that the selected APK:\n\n\342\227\217   Exists.\n\342\227\217   Is a regular file.\n\342\227\217   Is not empty.\n\342\227\217   Has the .apk extension.\n\342\227\217   Is exactly app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk.\nUpload the GitHub Actions artifact\nAfter APK verification, add a step named:\nUpload debug APK artifact\nUse actions/upload-artifact.\nUpload only:\napp/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\nName the artifact exactly:\napp-debug-apk\nConfigure artifact upload to fail when the APK is missing.\nDo not upload a directory containing unrelated files.\nDo not upload:\n\342\227\217   debug.keystore\n\342\227\217   Credentials\n\342\227\217   Source code\n\342\227\217   Gradle caches\n\342\227\217   Build caches\n\342\227\217   Configuration files\n\342\227\217   Secrets\n\342\227\217   Logs containing sensitive information\n\342\227\217   google-services.json\n\342\227\217   Firebase configuration files\n\342\227\217   Signing files\nThe normal GitHub Actions artifact must remain available even after GitHub Release publishing\nis added.\nPrepare the APK release asset\n\nAfter the Actions artifact has been uploaded successfully, add a step named:\nPrepare APK release asset\nThat step must:\n\342\227\217   Create a temporary directory inside the GitHub Actions runner for the release asset.\n\342\227\217   Do not create or commit this directory in the repository.\n\342\227\217   Copy only the verified APK into that temporary directory.\n\342\227\217   Give the copied APK a clear filename based on the repository name and workflow run\nnumber.\n\342\227\217   Sanitize the repository name before using it in the filename.\n\342\227\217   Use only safe filename characters.\n\342\227\217   Preserve the .apk extension.\n\342\227\217   Do not compress the APK.\n\342\227\217   Do not place the APK inside a ZIP file.\n\342\227\217   Do not rename any file inside the repository.\n\342\227\217   Do not modify the original APK.\n\342\227\217   Export the final release-asset path through GITHUB_OUTPUT for the release step.\nUse a release filename in this general format:\nrepository-name-debug-build-run-number.apk\nFor example:\nmy-android-app-debug-build-12.apk\nDo not hard-code a specific app name or repository name.\nPublish the APK to GitHub Releases\nAfter the normal Actions artifact has been uploaded and the release asset has been prepared,\nadd a step named:\nPublish APK to GitHub Releases\nUse the GitHub CLI command:\ngh release create\nDo not use an unverified third-party GitHub Release action.\nAuthenticate GitHub CLI using:\nGH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n\nBefore attempting release creation:\n\342\227\217   Run gh --version.\n\342\227\217   Confirm that GitHub CLI is available.\n\342\227\217   Confirm that the prepared release asset exists.\n\342\227\217   Confirm that the release asset is a non-empty .apk file.\n\342\227\217   Do not attempt release creation if APK validation fails.\nUnique release tag\nCreate a unique tag for every workflow execution using both:\n\342\227\217   GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER\n\342\227\217   GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT\nUse this tag format:\ndebug-apk-build-GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER-GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT\nFor example:\ndebug-apk-build-12-1\nConstruct the tag dynamically at workflow runtime.\nDo not use a fixed tag such as:\n\342\227\217   latest\n\342\227\217   debug\n\342\227\217   build\n\342\227\217   v1\n\342\227\217   apk\nDo not overwrite, move, delete, or reuse an existing release tag.\nThe unique tag must prevent a release conflict when:\n\342\227\217   A new commit is pushed.\n\342\227\217   The workflow is run manually.\n\342\227\217   A failed workflow is rerun.\n\342\227\217   The same workflow run is attempted again.\nRelease contents\nCreate a published GitHub Release with:\n\nRelease title:\nDebug APK Build #GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER\nRelease tag:\ndebug-apk-build-GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER-GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT\nTarget commit:\nGITHUB_SHA\nRelease notes that clearly state:\n\342\227\217   This is an automatically generated debug APK.\n\342\227\217   The APK was built by GitHub Actions.\n\342\227\217   The GitHub Actions run number.\n\342\227\217   The GitHub Actions run attempt.\n\342\227\217   The source commit SHA.\n\342\227\217   The APK is intended for testing.\n\342\227\217   The APK is not a Play Store production release.\n\342\227\217   The APK is signed only with a temporary debug keystore.\nAttach only the prepared .apk file as the manually uploaded release asset.\nDo not manually attach:\n\342\227\217   A ZIP file\n\342\227\217   A source-code archive\n\342\227\217   A tar.gz file\n\342\227\217   The debug keystore\n\342\227\217   Credentials\n\342\227\217   Configuration files\n\342\227\217   Gradle files\n\342\227\217   Build caches\n\342\227\217   Logs\n\342\227\217   Secrets\n\342\227\217   Any APK other than the verified app debug APK\nGitHub may automatically display its standard Source code (zip) and Source code (tar.gz) links\nfor the release. Do not attempt to create, upload, replace, remove, or modify those\nplatform-generated links.\nMark the newly created release explicitly as the latest release using:\n--latest\n\nDo not create the release as:\n\342\227\217   A draft\n\342\227\217   A prerelease\n\342\227\217   An immutable release requiring later manual publication\nThe APK must be visible directly under the release Assets section after successful publishing.\nRelease failure protection\nThe GitHub Actions artifact must be uploaded before release publishing begins.\nConfigure the release publishing step so that:\n\342\227\217   A release error does not remove or hide the successfully uploaded Actions artifact.\n\342\227\217   A release error does not cause the APK build result to be lost.\n\342\227\217   A release error is shown clearly as a warning.\n\342\227\217   The workflow summary clearly reports that the APK build and artifact upload succeeded\neven when release publishing fails.\n\342\227\217   The workflow does not falsely report that release publishing succeeded.\n\342\227\217   The release step uses continue-on-error: true.\n\342\227\217   No unrelated fallback release action is attempted.\n\342\227\217   No duplicate release is created as a fallback.\nAssign an id to the release step so its outcome can be checked later.\nVerify the release result\nAfter the release attempt, add a step named:\nReport APK download result\nThis step must always run after the release attempt.\nIf release publishing succeeded:\n\342\227\217   Confirm the release using gh release view.\n\342\227\217   Print the release tag.\n\342\227\217   Print the release title.\n\342\227\217   Print the direct GitHub Release page URL.\n\342\227\217   Print the exact APK asset filename.\n\342\227\217   Add the release page URL to GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY.\n\342\227\217   Add a message explaining that the APK can be downloaded from the release Assets\nsection.\n\342\227\217   State that the normal Actions artifact is also available as a backup.\n\nIf release publishing failed:\n\342\227\217   Print a clear warning.\n\342\227\217   State that the APK build succeeded.\n\342\227\217   State that the Actions artifact named app-debug-apk remains available.\n\342\227\217   Add the same warning and backup instructions to GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY.\n\342\227\217   Do not falsely print a release URL.\n\342\227\217   Do not fail the completed APK build solely because release publishing failed.\nAuthenticate any gh command in this reporting step using:\nGH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\nSecurity restrictions\nDo not create fake:\n\342\227\217   google-services.json files\n\342\227\217   Firebase files\n\342\227\217   API keys\n\342\227\217   Credentials\n\342\227\217   Personal access tokens\n\342\227\217   Release-signing files\n\342\227\217   Production keystores\n\342\227\217   Missing secrets\n\342\227\217   Placeholder secrets\nDo not expose:\n\342\227\217   GITHUB_TOKEN\n\342\227\217   GH_TOKEN\n\342\227\217   Environment credentials\n\342\227\217   Repository secrets\n\342\227\217   Keystore contents\nDo not echo authentication tokens into workflow logs.\nDo not persist credentials beyond the temporary GitHub Actions runner.\nDo not modify repository settings.\nDo not enable GitHub Pages.\nDo not create a website.\nDo not create a second workflow.\n\nDo not create a release manually while preparing the repository.\nThe release must be created only when the generated workflow runs after I manually commit\nand push the workflow file.\nFinal validation before finishing\nBefore finishing, confirm all of the following:\n\342\227\217   Only .github/workflows/build-apk.yml was created.\n\342\227\217   No existing file was modified.\n\342\227\217   AGP 9.1.1 was confirmed from gradle/libs.versions.toml.\n\342\227\217   Java 17 is configured before Gradle.\n\342\227\217   The active Java version is verified.\n\342\227\217   Gradle 9.3.1 is used exactly.\n\342\227\217   The repository Gradle wrapper is not used.\n\342\227\217   The temporary debug keystore is created before the build.\n\342\227\217   The temporary debug keystore is never uploaded.\n\342\227\217   The build command is exactly gradle :app:assembleDebug --stacktrace --no-daemon.\n\342\227\217   The APK path is exactly app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk.\n\342\227\217   The Actions artifact name is exactly app-debug-apk.\n\342\227\217   actions/upload-artifact is configured to fail when the APK is missing.\n\342\227\217   The Actions artifact is uploaded before release publishing.\n\342\227\217   The release asset is an actual .apk file and not a ZIP.\n\342\227\217   Every workflow execution receives a unique release tag.\n\342\227\217   GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER and GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT are both used in the tag.\n\342\227\217   The release targets GITHUB_SHA.\n\342\227\217   The release is explicitly marked as latest.\n\342\227\217   The built-in GitHub token is used.\n\342\227\217   The workflow has contents: write permission.\n\342\227\217   No personal access token or repository secret is required.\n\342\227\217   Release failure does not remove the Actions artifact.\n\342\227\217   The workflow summary reports whether release publishing succeeded or failed.\n\342\227\217   No Android application or project file was modified.\n\342\227\217   No file other than .github/workflows/build-apk.yml was created.\nGive me a short workflow summary that includes:\n\342\227\217   The confirmed AGP version.\n\342\227\217   The Java version requirement.\n\342\227\217   The exact Gradle version.\n\342\227\217   The exact build command.\n\342\227\217   The APK path.\n\342\227\217   The Actions artifact name.\n\n\342\227\217   The release tag format.\n\342\227\217   The release asset filename format.\n\342\227\217   Confirmation that the latest successful release will contain a directly downloadable APK.\n\342\227\217   Confirmation that release failure will leave the Actions artifact available.\nDo not publish, commit, sync, push, tag, or create a GitHub Release now.\nWait for me to manually commit and push the workflow file to GitHub."
    items {
      text: "Prepare this completed Google AI Studio Android app for automatic debug APK building and\nGitHub Release publishing with GitHub Actions.\nBefore creating anything, confirm that:\ngradle/libs.versions.toml\ncontains exactly:\nagp = \"9.1.1\"\nIf the AGP version is not exactly 9.1.1:\n\342\227\217   Stop immediately.\n\342\227\217   Report the detected AGP value.\n\342\227\217   Do not create the workflow.\n\342\227\217   Do not modify any file.\nIf the AGP version is exactly 9.1.1, create only:\n.github/workflows/build-apk.yml\nDo not create, edit, delete, rename, format, upgrade, or replace any other repository file.\n\nDo not modify the Android app, source code, design, features, package name, application ID,\nmanifest, resources, dependencies, Gradle project files, signing configuration, or project\nsettings.\nThe workflow must build the debug APK, preserve it as a normal GitHub Actions artifact, and\npublish the same APK directly under GitHub Releases for easy downloading on a phone.\nWorkflow triggers\nCreate a GitHub Actions workflow that:\n\342\227\217   Runs automatically on every push to the main branch.\n\342\227\217   Also supports workflow_dispatch.\n\342\227\217   Does not run on pull requests.\n\342\227\217   Uses ubuntu-latest.\n\342\227\217   Checks out the complete repository.\n\342\227\217   Runs all Gradle commands from the repository root.\nWorkflow permissions\nAdd only the permission required to create a GitHub Release:\npermissions:\ncontents: write\nDo not request unnecessary permissions.\nDo not use a personal access token, repository secret, external API key, deployment key, or\ncustom credential.\nUse only the workflow\'s built-in GitHub token for release creation:\n${{ github.token }}\nJava setup\nSet up Temurin Java 17 using actions/setup-java.\nJava must be configured before Gradle is configured or any Gradle command is executed.\nAdd a step named:\nVerify Java environment\n\nThat step must:\n\342\227\217   Run java -version.\n\342\227\217   Print JAVA_HOME.\n\342\227\217   Detect the active Java major version.\n\342\227\217   Confirm that the active Java major version is 17 or newer.\n\342\227\217   Fail clearly if Java is lower than 17.\n\342\227\217   Fail clearly if the Java version cannot be detected.\nGradle setup\nSet up exactly Gradle 9.3.1 using gradle/actions/setup-gradle.\nDo not use:\n\342\227\217   Gradle 8.13\n\342\227\217   The repository Gradle wrapper\n\342\227\217   latest\n\342\227\217   current\n\342\227\217   release-candidate\n\342\227\217   nightly\n\342\227\217   Any Gradle version other than exactly 9.3.1\nRun all Gradle commands from the repository root.\nTemporary debug keystore\nBefore building, add a step named:\nCreate temporary debug keystore\nThat step must:\n\342\227\217   Check whether ./debug.keystore already exists.\n\342\227\217   Generate it only when it is missing.\n\342\227\217   Use keytool from the configured Java 17 installation.\n\342\227\217   Use exactly:\n\342\227\213   Keystore password: android\n\342\227\213   Key alias: androiddebugkey\n\342\227\213   Key password: android\n\342\227\213   Distinguished name: CN=Android Debug,O=Android,C=US\n\342\227\213   Algorithm: RSA\n\342\227\213   Key size: 2048\n\342\227\213   Validity: 10000 days\n\n\342\227\217   Confirm that ./debug.keystore exists after generation.\n\342\227\217   Fail clearly if the keystore cannot be created.\n\342\227\217   Never commit the keystore.\n\342\227\217   Never cache the keystore.\n\342\227\217   Never print the keystore.\n\342\227\217   Never expose the keystore.\n\342\227\217   Never preserve the keystore after the workflow runner is removed.\n\342\227\217   Never upload the keystore as an artifact or release asset.\nBuild the debug APK\nBuild the debug APK using exactly:\ngradle :app:assembleDebug --stacktrace --no-daemon\nDo not replace this command with:\n\342\227\217   ./gradlew\n\342\227\217   gradlew\n\342\227\217   assembleRelease\n\342\227\217   bundleRelease\n\342\227\217   assemble\n\342\227\217   build\n\342\227\217   Any other Gradle command\nVerify the APK\nAfter the build, verify that this exact file exists:\napp/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\nIf the exact file is missing:\n\342\227\217   Search only inside app/build/outputs/apk.\n\342\227\217   Print the APK paths discovered inside that directory.\n\342\227\217   Do not search the entire repository.\n\342\227\217   Do not select a release APK.\n\342\227\217   Do not select an Android test APK.\n\342\227\217   Do not select an APK from another module.\n\342\227\217   Do not upload or release an unrelated APK.\n\342\227\217   Fail clearly if the expected debug APK does not exist.\nConfirm that the selected APK:\n\n\342\227\217   Exists.\n\342\227\217   Is a regular file.\n\342\227\217   Is not empty.\n\342\227\217   Has the .apk extension.\n\342\227\217   Is exactly app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk.\nUpload the GitHub Actions artifact\nAfter APK verification, add a step named:\nUpload debug APK artifact\nUse actions/upload-artifact.\nUpload only:\napp/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\nName the artifact exactly:\napp-debug-apk\nConfigure artifact upload to fail when the APK is missing.\nDo not upload a directory containing unrelated files.\nDo not upload:\n\342\227\217   debug.keystore\n\342\227\217   Credentials\n\342\227\217   Source code\n\342\227\217   Gradle caches\n\342\227\217   Build caches\n\342\227\217   Configuration files\n\342\227\217   Secrets\n\342\227\217   Logs containing sensitive information\n\342\227\217   google-services.json\n\342\227\217   Firebase configuration files\n\342\227\217   Signing files\nThe normal GitHub Actions artifact must remain available even after GitHub Release publishing\nis added.\nPrepare the APK release asset\n\nAfter the Actions artifact has been uploaded successfully, add a step named:\nPrepare APK release asset\nThat step must:\n\342\227\217   Create a temporary directory inside the GitHub Actions runner for the release asset.\n\342\227\217   Do not create or commit this directory in the repository.\n\342\227\217   Copy only the verified APK into that temporary directory.\n\342\227\217   Give the copied APK a clear filename based on the repository name and workflow run\nnumber.\n\342\227\217   Sanitize the repository name before using it in the filename.\n\342\227\217   Use only safe filename characters.\n\342\227\217   Preserve the .apk extension.\n\342\227\217   Do not compress the APK.\n\342\227\217   Do not place the APK inside a ZIP file.\n\342\227\217   Do not rename any file inside the repository.\n\342\227\217   Do not modify the original APK.\n\342\227\217   Export the final release-asset path through GITHUB_OUTPUT for the release step.\nUse a release filename in this general format:\nrepository-name-debug-build-run-number.apk\nFor example:\nmy-android-app-debug-build-12.apk\nDo not hard-code a specific app name or repository name.\nPublish the APK to GitHub Releases\nAfter the normal Actions artifact has been uploaded and the release asset has been prepared,\nadd a step named:\nPublish APK to GitHub Releases\nUse the GitHub CLI command:\ngh release create\nDo not use an unverified third-party GitHub Release action.\nAuthenticate GitHub CLI using:\nGH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n\nBefore attempting release creation:\n\342\227\217   Run gh --version.\n\342\227\217   Confirm that GitHub CLI is available.\n\342\227\217   Confirm that the prepared release asset exists.\n\342\227\217   Confirm that the release asset is a non-empty .apk file.\n\342\227\217   Do not attempt release creation if APK validation fails.\nUnique release tag\nCreate a unique tag for every workflow execution using both:\n\342\227\217   GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER\n\342\227\217   GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT\nUse this tag format:\ndebug-apk-build-GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER-GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT\nFor example:\ndebug-apk-build-12-1\nConstruct the tag dynamically at workflow runtime.\nDo not use a fixed tag such as:\n\342\227\217   latest\n\342\227\217   debug\n\342\227\217   build\n\342\227\217   v1\n\342\227\217   apk\nDo not overwrite, move, delete, or reuse an existing release tag.\nThe unique tag must prevent a release conflict when:\n\342\227\217   A new commit is pushed.\n\342\227\217   The workflow is run manually.\n\342\227\217   A failed workflow is rerun.\n\342\227\217   The same workflow run is attempted again.\nRelease contents\nCreate a published GitHub Release with:\n\nRelease title:\nDebug APK Build #GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER\nRelease tag:\ndebug-apk-build-GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER-GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT\nTarget commit:\nGITHUB_SHA\nRelease notes that clearly state:\n\342\227\217   This is an automatically generated debug APK.\n\342\227\217   The APK was built by GitHub Actions.\n\342\227\217   The GitHub Actions run number.\n\342\227\217   The GitHub Actions run attempt.\n\342\227\217   The source commit SHA.\n\342\227\217   The APK is intended for testing.\n\342\227\217   The APK is not a Play Store production release.\n\342\227\217   The APK is signed only with a temporary debug keystore.\nAttach only the prepared .apk file as the manually uploaded release asset.\nDo not manually attach:\n\342\227\217   A ZIP file\n\342\227\217   A source-code archive\n\342\227\217   A tar.gz file\n\342\227\217   The debug keystore\n\342\227\217   Credentials\n\342\227\217   Configuration files\n\342\227\217   Gradle files\n\342\227\217   Build caches\n\342\227\217   Logs\n\342\227\217   Secrets\n\342\227\217   Any APK other than the verified app debug APK\nGitHub may automatically display its standard Source code (zip) and Source code (tar.gz) links\nfor the release. Do not attempt to create, upload, replace, remove, or modify those\nplatform-generated links.\nMark the newly created release explicitly as the latest release using:\n--latest\n\nDo not create the release as:\n\342\227\217   A draft\n\342\227\217   A prerelease\n\342\227\217   An immutable release requiring later manual publication\nThe APK must be visible directly under the release Assets section after successful publishing.\nRelease failure protection\nThe GitHub Actions artifact must be uploaded before release publishing begins.\nConfigure the release publishing step so that:\n\342\227\217   A release error does not remove or hide the successfully uploaded Actions artifact.\n\342\227\217   A release error does not cause the APK build result to be lost.\n\342\227\217   A release error is shown clearly as a warning.\n\342\227\217   The workflow summary clearly reports that the APK build and artifact upload succeeded\neven when release publishing fails.\n\342\227\217   The workflow does not falsely report that release publishing succeeded.\n\342\227\217   The release step uses continue-on-error: true.\n\342\227\217   No unrelated fallback release action is attempted.\n\342\227\217   No duplicate release is created as a fallback.\nAssign an id to the release step so its outcome can be checked later.\nVerify the release result\nAfter the release attempt, add a step named:\nReport APK download result\nThis step must always run after the release attempt.\nIf release publishing succeeded:\n\342\227\217   Confirm the release using gh release view.\n\342\227\217   Print the release tag.\n\342\227\217   Print the release title.\n\342\227\217   Print the direct GitHub Release page URL.\n\342\227\217   Print the exact APK asset filename.\n\342\227\217   Add the release page URL to GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY.\n\342\227\217   Add a message explaining that the APK can be downloaded from the release Assets\nsection.\n\342\227\217   State that the normal Actions artifact is also available as a backup.\n\nIf release publishing failed:\n\342\227\217   Print a clear warning.\n\342\227\217   State that the APK build succeeded.\n\342\227\217   State that the Actions artifact named app-debug-apk remains available.\n\342\227\217   Add the same warning and backup instructions to GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY.\n\342\227\217   Do not falsely print a release URL.\n\342\227\217   Do not fail the completed APK build solely because release publishing failed.\nAuthenticate any gh command in this reporting step using:\nGH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\nSecurity restrictions\nDo not create fake:\n\342\227\217   google-services.json files\n\342\227\217   Firebase files\n\342\227\217   API keys\n\342\227\217   Credentials\n\342\227\217   Personal access tokens\n\342\227\217   Release-signing files\n\342\227\217   Production keystores\n\342\227\217   Missing secrets\n\342\227\217   Placeholder secrets\nDo not expose:\n\342\227\217   GITHUB_TOKEN\n\342\227\217   GH_TOKEN\n\342\227\217   Environment credentials\n\342\227\217   Repository secrets\n\342\227\217   Keystore contents\nDo not echo authentication tokens into workflow logs.\nDo not persist credentials beyond the temporary GitHub Actions runner.\nDo not modify repository settings.\nDo not enable GitHub Pages.\nDo not create a website.\nDo not create a second workflow.\n\nDo not create a release manually while preparing the repository.\nThe release must be created only when the generated workflow runs after I manually commit\nand push the workflow file.\nFinal validation before finishing\nBefore finishing, confirm all of the following:\n\342\227\217   Only .github/workflows/build-apk.yml was created.\n\342\227\217   No existing file was modified.\n\342\227\217   AGP 9.1.1 was confirmed from gradle/libs.versions.toml.\n\342\227\217   Java 17 is configured before Gradle.\n\342\227\217   The active Java version is verified.\n\342\227\217   Gradle 9.3.1 is used exactly.\n\342\227\217   The repository Gradle wrapper is not used.\n\342\227\217   The temporary debug keystore is created before the build.\n\342\227\217   The temporary debug keystore is never uploaded.\n\342\227\217   The build command is exactly gradle :app:assembleDebug --stacktrace --no-daemon.\n\342\227\217   The APK path is exactly app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk.\n\342\227\217   The Actions artifact name is exactly app-debug-apk.\n\342\227\217   actions/upload-artifact is configured to fail when the APK is missing.\n\342\227\217   The Actions artifact is uploaded before release publishing.\n\342\227\217   The release asset is an actual .apk file and not a ZIP.\n\342\227\217   Every workflow execution receives a unique release tag.\n\342\227\217   GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER and GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT are both used in the tag.\n\342\227\217   The release targets GITHUB_SHA.\n\342\227\217   The release is explicitly marked as latest.\n\342\227\217   The built-in GitHub token is used.\n\342\227\217   The workflow has contents: write permission.\n\342\227\217   No personal access token or repository secret is required.\n\342\227\217   Release failure does not remove the Actions artifact.\n\342\227\217   The workflow summary reports whether release publishing succeeded or failed.\n\342\227\217   No Android application or project file was modified.\n\342\227\217   No file other than .github/workflows/build-apk.yml was created.\nGive me a short workflow summary that includes:\n\342\227\217   The confirmed AGP version.\n\342\227\217   The Java version requirement.\n\342\227\217   The exact Gradle version.\n\342\227\217   The exact build command.\n\342\227\217   The APK path.\n\342\227\217   The Actions artifact name.\n\n\342\227\217   The release tag format.\n\342\227\217   The release asset filename format.\n\342\227\217   Confirmation that the latest successful release will contain a directly downloadable APK.\n\342\227\217   Confirmation that release failure will leave the Actions artifact available.\nDo not publish, commit, sync, push, tag, or create a GitHub Release now.\nWait for me to manually commit and push the workflow file to GitHub."
    }
  }
}
