  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "This summary captures the current state of the \"Easy App\" development, an accessible Android launcher designed for seniors, featuring Gemini-powered voice assistance, emergency SOS capabilities, and accessibility-based WhatsApp automation.\n\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n*   **Create GitHub Actions Workflow:** Create `.github/workflows/build-apk.yml` for automatic debug APK building and GitHub Release publishing.\n    *   **Status:** NOT STARTED.\n    *   **Intent:** The user provided strict requirements for this workflow:\n        *   Trigger on push to `main` (no PRs), support `workflow_dispatch`.\n        *   Use `ubuntu-latest`, Java 17 (Temurin), and Gradle 9.3.1.\n        *   Generate a temporary debug keystore (`androiddebugkey`).\n        *   Build command: `gradle :app:assembleDebug --stacktrace --no-daemon`.\n        *   Verify APK at `app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk`.\n        *   Upload artifact `app-debug-apk`.\n        *   Publish to GitHub Releases using `gh release create` with a unique tag format (`debug-apk-build-RUN_NUMBER-RUN_ATTEMPT`).\n        *   Use `permissions: contents: write` and `${{ github.token }}`.\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n\n*   **Preferences/Rules:**\n    *   The app must remain accessible, high-contrast, and senior-friendly.\n    *   The build process must strictly adhere to the provided AGP version (9.1.1) and Gradle version (9.3.1).\n    *   No hardcoded secrets, personal access tokens, or production keystores are allowed in the workflow.\n*   **Context:**\n    *   The app uses `libs.versions.toml` for dependency management.\n    *   The user explicitly confirmed the AGP version is 9.1.1.\n    *   \"Prepare this completed Google AI Studio Android app for automatic debug APK building and GitHub Release publishing with GitHub Actions.\"\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n\n*   **Architecture Implementation:** Built a complete Android launcher with a custom Compose UI.\n*   **Voice Assistant:** Implemented `GeminiAssistantManager` using Gemini Function Calling to map natural language to system intents, with a local heuristic fallback for offline reliability.\n*   **Accessibility/Automation:**\n    *   Implemented `WhatsAppNotificationService` to intercept notifications and manage `RemoteInput` replies.\n    *   Implemented `WhatsAppAccessibilityFallbackService` to automate UI interactions (opening chats, sending messages) when direct notification replies aren\'t available.\n*   **Emergency System:** Implemented `SosManager` and `SosEmergencyForegroundService` to handle audio recording, transcription, GPS acquisition, and emergency dispatching via WhatsApp and SMS.\n*   **Build Configuration:** Verified AGP 9.1.1 in `gradle/libs.versions.toml`.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n\n*   **Architecture:**\n    *   `MainActivity.kt` orchestrates the UI and initializes core managers.\n    *   `NativeActionExecutor` bridges Gemini tool calls to Android system capabilities (SMS, Phone, Torch, etc.).\n    *   `SosEmergencyForegroundService` is a high-priority foreground service requiring `microphone` and `location` permissions.\n    *   `WhatsAppAccessibilityFallbackService` requires the `BIND_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICE` permission and specific XML configuration (`whatsapp_accessibility_config.xml`).\n*   **Constraints:**\n    *   The app relies on `NotificationListenerService` and `AccessibilityService` for its core automation features.\n    *   The build environment must be configured for Java 17 and Gradle 9.3.1.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n\n*   **Edited/Created Files:**\n    *   `/gradle/libs.versions.toml`: Confirmed AGP 9.1.1.\n    *   `/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`: Added necessary permissions and service declarations.\n    *   `/app/src/main/java/com/example/MainActivity.kt`: Main UI entry point, manages speech recognition and UI state.\n    *   `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ai/GeminiAssistantManager.kt`: Core AI logic and tool definitions.\n    *   `/app/src/main/java/com/example/accessibility/SosManager.kt`: SOS state machine.\n    *   `/app/src/main/java/com/example/services/SosEmergencyForegroundService.kt`: Emergency background task handler.\n    *   `/app/src/main/java/com/example/services/WhatsAppAccessibilityFallbackService.kt`: UI automation for WhatsApp.\n    *   `/app/src/main/java/com/example/notifications/WhatsAppNotificationService.kt`: Notification interception.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n*   **Immediate Next Step:** Create the `.github/workflows/build-apk.yml` file.\n*   **Instructions for Next Agent:**\n    1.  Read the strict requirements in the user\'s last message regarding the GitHub Actions workflow.\n    2.  Create `.github/workflows/build-apk.yml` exactly as specified.\n    3.  Ensure Java 17 setup and Gradle 9.3.1 setup are correctly ordered.\n    4.  Implement the temporary debug keystore generation step.\n    5.  Implement the build, verify, upload-artifact, and release publishing steps as defined.\n    6.  Do not modify any other project files."
