  file_change {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///.agents/skills/adaptive/references/android/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/flexbox/index.md"
    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    diff {
      unified_diff {
        lines {
          text: "> [!NOTE]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Note:** FlexBox is an experimental API and is likely to change in the future. To use it, annotate your code with `@ExperimentalFlexBoxApi`. Please file any issues or feedback on the [issue tracker](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/new?component=1876021&title=%5BFlexBox%5D)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[`FlexBox`](https://developer.android.com/reference/kotlin/androidx/compose/foundation/layout/FlexBox.composable#FlexBox(androidx.compose.ui.Modifier,androidx.compose.foundation.layout.FlexBoxConfig,kotlin.Function1)) is a container that lays out items in a single direction. It can"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "resize, wrap, align, and distribute space among items to optimally fill the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "available space. It\'s a useful layout for different sized items and for resizing"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "items when the available space changes."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "With `FlexBox`, you can:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Control how items grow and shrink to fill the available space"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Wrap items onto new rows or columns when there isn\'t enough space for them"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Distribute extra space between items using convenient presets"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## When to use FlexBox"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`FlexBox` is usually used to display a small number of items *within* an"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "overall screen layout. For an overall screen layout,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`Grid` is usually a better choice. `FlexBox` does not support lazy-loading of"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "items. To display large numbers of items, use [lazy lists and grids](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/lists). If you"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "need to wrap items, use `FlexBox` instead of `FlowRow` and `FlowColumn`."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Terminology and concepts"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> [!IMPORTANT]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Key Point:** `FlexBox` is heavily influenced by the [CSS Flexible Box Layout specification](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-flexbox-1/) and has almost identical concepts, terminology, and behavior. If you\'re familiar with `display: flex`, you\'ll find `FlexBox`\'s properties and behavior almost identical."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`FlexBox` lays out its items in either horizontal or vertical *lines* . This"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "direction of these lines establishes the *main axis* . 90 degrees to the main"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "axis is the *cross axis* . The length of the `FlexBox` along the main axis is"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "known as the *main size* . The corresponding cross axis length is known as the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "*cross size* . These sizes and axes form the basis of `FlexBox`\'s behavior."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![FlexBox with horizontal main axis and vertical cross axis.](https://developer.android.com/static/develop/ui/compose/images/layouts/adaptive/flexbox/intro-row-2.png) **Figure 1.** Axes and sizes when the `FlexBox` direction is `Row`. ![FlexBox with vertical main axis and horizontal cross axis.](https://developer.android.com/static/develop/ui/compose/images/layouts/adaptive/flexbox/intro-column.png) **Figure 2.** Axes and sizes when the `FlexBox` direction is `Column`."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "<br />"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Apply properties"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "You can apply `FlexBox` properties in two ways:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- To the `FlexBox` container using `FlexBox(config)`"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- To an item inside the `FlexBox` using `Modifier.flex`"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Container properties (`config`**) | **Item properties (`Modifier.flex`**) |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "|---|---|"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| - `direction` - the item layout direction - `wrap` - whether to wrap items if the **main size** is insufficient - `justifyContent` - how to **distribute** items along the **main axis** - `alignItems` - how to **align** items along the **cross axis** - `alignContent` - how to distribute extra space from the **cross size** when there are multiple lines - `rowGap` / `columnGap` - adds space between items and lines See [Set container behavior](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/flexbox/container-behavior) for more information about these properties. | - `basis` - the size of the item before any extra space from the **main size** is distributed - `grow` - the share of extra space from the **main size** that this item should receive - `shrink` - the share of space deficit from the **main size** that this item should receive - `alignSelf` - how to distribute extra space from the **cross size** to this item, overrides `alignItems` - `order` - controls the layout order See [Set item behavior](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/flexbox/item-behavior) for more information about these properties. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Understand the `FlexBox` layout algorithm"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "One of `FlexBox`\'s most powerful features is its ability to resize its children"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "to best fit the space available to it. Understanding how `FlexBox` does this can"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "help you set `FlexBox` properties to optimize your UI for all possible sizes."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`FlexBox`\'s layout algorithm works in the following way:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "1. **Calculate child base size** : Use the child\'s [`basis` value](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/flexbox/item-behavior#set-initial-size)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   to calculate its initial size along the main axis before any extra space is"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   distributed."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "2. **Sort the children** : Sort the children by their [`order`](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/flexbox/item-behavior#item-order) values, if"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   present."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "3. **Build lines** : For each child, check if its initial size plus"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   [`gap`](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/flexbox/container-behavior#add-gaps) will fit into the remaining space on the current line."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   If so, place this child into the line. If not, place it onto a new line if"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   [wrapping is enabled](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/flexbox/container-behavior#wrap-items), or place the item into the current line"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   where it will overflow (it will be partially obscured by the edge of the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   container)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "4. **Align or resize items in the main axis** : For each line, distribute extra"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   space *to* or between items by [resizing](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/flexbox/item-behavior#item-size) or"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   [aligning](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/flexbox/container-behavior#main-axis) them."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "5. **Align or resize items in the cross axis** : For each line, distribute extra"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   space to or between items and lines by [stretching or aligning"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   them](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/flexbox/container-behavior#cross-axis)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Now that you\'re familiar with `FlexBox` concepts, see [Get started](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/flexbox/get-started) to"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "create a basic `FlexBox`."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
