          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "<br />"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Define grid areas with named areas"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Named areas allow you to attach names to groups of grid cells,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "which are called [grid areas](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/grid#grid-area)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "You can use these names instead of [coordinate indexes](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/grid/item-properties#position)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "when placing UI elements in the grid."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Using named areas has two main benefits to code readability:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- When defining the grid layout, the purpose and placement of the expected content is clear."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- When adding the content, the purpose of that content is clear."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "To organize complex layouts clearly, you can decouple your physical grid"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "structure from child placement by defining semantic grid areas."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Inside the `config` lambda, use the [`area`](https://developer.android.com/reference/kotlin/androidx/compose/foundation/layout/GridConfigurationScope#area(kotlin.Any,kotlin.Int,kotlin.Int,kotlin.Int,kotlin.Int)) function in"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`GridConfigurationScope` to register named areas in the grid."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "You can then assign child composables to these areas"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "using the [`gridItem`](https://developer.android.com/reference/kotlin/androidx/compose/foundation/layout/GridScope#(androidx.compose.ui.Modifier).gridItem(kotlin.Any,androidx.compose.ui.Alignment)) modifier"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "with the corresponding area identifier. The `area` function maps"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "a semantic identifier (such as an `enum` class value or a string key) to"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "a set of physical grid coordinates. Grid lines and indexes are **1-based**"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "(that is, the first row is `1`, and the first column is `1`)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "For example, you define a grid that has four area IDs:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "/**"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: " * An enum representing the IDs for named areas within the grid."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: " */"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "enum class GridAreaNames {"
