  file_change {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///.agents/skills/adaptive/references/android/develop/ui/compose/layouts/adaptive/grid/index.md"
    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    diff {
      unified_diff {
        lines {
          text: "> [!NOTE]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Note:** `Grid` is an experimental API and is subject to change. File any issues on the [issue tracker](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/new?component=1876021&template=1424126)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[`Grid`](https://developer.android.com/reference/kotlin/androidx/compose/foundation/layout/Grid.composable#Grid(kotlin.Function1,androidx.compose.ui.Modifier,kotlin.Function1)) is a Jetpack Compose API"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "that lets you flexibly implement a two-dimensional layout."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "With this API, you can display items in multi-column"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "or multi-row layouts that adapt to the available container size."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![A flexible and adaptive two-dimensional layout with Grid](https://developer.android.com/static/develop/ui/compose/images/layouts/adaptive/grid/example.png) **Figure 1.** A flexible and adaptive two-dimensional layout with `Grid`."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## How is Grid different from similar composables?"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Compose already offers similar components, such as [`LazyVerticalGrid`](https://developer.android.com/reference/kotlin/androidx/compose/foundation/lazy/grid/LazyVerticalGrid.composable#LazyVerticalGrid(androidx.compose.foundation.lazy.grid.GridCells,androidx.compose.ui.Modifier,androidx.compose.foundation.lazy.grid.LazyGridState,androidx.compose.foundation.layout.PaddingValues,kotlin.Boolean,androidx.compose.foundation.layout.Arrangement.Vertical,androidx.compose.foundation.layout.Arrangement.Horizontal,androidx.compose.foundation.gestures.FlingBehavior,kotlin.Boolean,androidx.compose.foundation.OverscrollEffect,kotlin.Function1))."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "These components are mainly for visualization of large, homogeneous data sets---"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "for example, displaying a content catalog in a video streaming app."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "These components are NOT designed"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "for the structural layout of a screen or complex component."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "You can also implement a two-dimensional layout"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "by combining multiple `Row` and `Column` composables."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "However, this approach has some downsides,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "such as deep hierarchies and difficulties in adaptability."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The following table provides an overview"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "of which layouts are suitable for each API:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| Component | Purpose |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "|---|---|"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| `LazyVerticalGrid`, `LazyStaggeredGrid`, `LazyHorizontalGrid` | Visualization of large, homogeneous data sets that require lazy loading. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| `Row`, `Column`, `FlexBox` | One-dimensional layout |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| `Grid` | Two-dimensional layout |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> [!NOTE]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Note:** `Grid` doesn\'t support lazy loading."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Terminology"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Familiarize yourself with the following terminology"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "to understand how `Grid` works."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Grid line"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "A grid is made up of lines, which run horizontally and vertically."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "If your grid has three rows, it has four horizontal lines,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "including the one after the last row."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "In the following image, each dotted line represents a grid line:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![The grid consists of four horizontal lines and three vertical lines.](https://developer.android.com/static/develop/ui/compose/images/layouts/adaptive/grid/grid-line.png) **Figure 2**. The grid consists of four horizontal lines and three vertical lines."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Grid track"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "A grid track is the space between two grid lines."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "A row track is between two horizontal lines,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "and a column track is between two vertical lines."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "To define the size of these tracks,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "assign a size to them when you create the grid."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![A grid track for the first row.](https://developer.android.com/static/develop/ui/compose/images/layouts/adaptive/grid/grid-track.png) **Figure 3**. A grid track for the first row."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Grid cell"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "A grid cell is the intersection of a row and column track."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![A grid cell that is an intersection of the second row and the second column.](https://developer.android.com/static/develop/ui/compose/images/layouts/adaptive/grid/grid-cell.png) **Figure 4**. A grid cell that is an intersection of the second row and the second column."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Grid area"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "A grid area consists of several grid cells."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "You can define a grid area by making an item span multiple tracks."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![A grid area that consists of four grid cells.](https://developer.android.com/static/develop/ui/compose/images/layouts/adaptive/grid/grid-area.png) **Figure 5**. A grid area that consists of four grid cells."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Grid gap"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "A grid gap is the gutter between grid tracks."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "You can\'t place a UI element into a gap,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "but you can span a UI element across it."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![A grid gap between the first column and the second column.](https://developer.android.com/static/develop/ui/compose/images/layouts/adaptive/grid/grid-gap.png) **Figure 6**. A grid gap between the first column and the second column."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
