    diff {
      unified_diff {
        lines {
          text: "Tools for debugging your Compose UI are available in Android Studio."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Layout Inspector"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Layout Inspector lets you inspect a Compose layout inside a running app in an"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "emulator or physical device. You can use the Layout Inspector to check how often"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "a composable is recomposed or skipped, which can help identify issues with your"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "app. For example, some coding errors might force your UI to recompose"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "excessively, which can cause [poor performance](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/performance)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Some coding errors can prevent your UI from recomposing and, therefore,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "prevent your UI changes from showing up on the screen. If you\'re new to"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Layout inspector, check the [guidance](https://developer.android.com/studio/debug/layout-inspector) on how to"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "run it."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> [!NOTE]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Note:** If you\'re not seeing Compose components in layout inspector, make sure you are not removing `META-INF/androidx.compose.*.version` files from the APK. These are required for layout inspector to work."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Get recomposition counts"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "When debugging your Compose layouts, knowing when composables"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[recompose](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/mental-model#recomposition) is important in"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "understanding whether your UI is implemented properly. For example, if it\'s"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "recomposing too many times, your app might be doing more work than is necessary."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "On the other hand, components that don\'t recompose when you anticipate them to"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "can lead to unexpected behaviors."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The Layout Inspector shows you when discrete composables in your layout"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "hierarchy have either recomposed or skipped, as you interact with your app. In"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Android Studio, your recompositions are highlighted to help you determine"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "where in the UI your composables are recomposing."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Figure 1.** Recompositions are highlighted in Layout Inspector."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The highlighted portion shows a gradient overlay of the composable in the image"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "section of the Layout Inspector, and gradually disappears so that you can get an"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "idea of where in the UI the composable with the highest recompositions can be"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "found. If one composable is recomposing at a higher rate than another"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "composable, then the first composable receives a stronger gradient overlay"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "color. If you double-click a composable in the layout inspector, you\'re taken to"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "the corresponding code for analysis."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> [!NOTE]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Note:** To view recomposition counts, make sure your app is using an API level of 29 or higher, and `Compose 1.2.0` or higher. Then, deploy your app as you normally would."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![](https://developer.android.com/static/develop/ui/compose/images/li-recomposition-counts.png) **Figure 2.**The composition and skip counter in Layout Inspector."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Open the **Layout Inspector** window and connect to your app process. In the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Component Tree** , there are two columns that appear next to the layout"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "hierarchy. The first column shows the number of compositions for each node and"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "the second column displays the number of skips for each node. Selecting a"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "composable node shows the dimensions and parameters of the composable, unless"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "it\'s an inline function, in which case the parameters can\'t be shown. You can"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "also see similar information in the **Attributes** pane when you select a"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "composable from the **Component Tree** or the **Layout Display**."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Resetting the count can help you understand recompositions or skips during a"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "specific interaction with your app. If you want to reset the count, click"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Reset** near the top of the **Component Tree** pane."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> [!NOTE]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Note:** If you don\'t see the new columns in the **Component Tree** pane, you can view them by selecting **Show Recomposition Counts** from the **View Options** menu ![Layout Inspector View Options"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> icon](https://developer.android.com/static/studio/images/buttons/live-layout-inspector-view-options-icon.png) near the top of the **Component Tree** pane, as shown in the following image."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![Enable the composition and skip counter in Layout"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Inspector](https://developer.android.com/static/develop/ui/compose/images/li-show-recomposition-counts.png)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Figure 3**. Enable the composition and skip counter in Layout Inspector."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Compose semantics"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "In Compose, [Semantics](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/accessibility/semantics) describe your UI in an"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "alternative manner that is understandable for"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[Accessibility](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/accessibility) services and for the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[Testing](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/testing) framework. You can use the Layout Inspector"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "to inspect semantic information in your Compose layouts."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![Semantic information displayed using the Layout Inspector.](https://developer.android.com/static/develop/ui/compose/images/layout_inspector_semantics_new.png) **Figure 4.** Semantic information displayed using the Layout Inspector."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "When selecting a Compose node, use the **Attributes** pane to check whether it"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "declares semantic information directly, merges semantics from its children, or"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "both. To quickly identify which nodes include semantics, either declared or"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "merged, use select the **View options** drop-down in the **Component Tree** pane"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "and select **Highlight Semantics Layers**. This highlights only the nodes in the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "tree that include semantics, and you can use your keyboard to quickly navigate"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "between them."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Compose UI Check"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "To help you build more adaptive and accessible UIs in Jetpack Compose, Android"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Studio provides a UI Check mode in Compose Preview. This feature is similar"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "to [Accessibility Scanner](https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/accessibility/testing#accessibility-scanner)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "for views."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "When you activate Compose UI check mode on a Compose Preview, Android Studio"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "automatically audits your Compose UI and suggests improvements to make your UI"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "more accessible and adaptive. Android Studio checks that your UI works across"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "different screen sizes. In the **Problems** panel, the tool shows the issues"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "that it detects, such as text stretched on large screens or low color contrast."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "To access this feature, click the UI Check icon on Compose Preview:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![](https://developer.android.com/static/studio/images/design/compose-ui-check-entry.png) **Figure 5.** Entry point to UI check mode."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "UI check automatically previews your UI in different configurations and"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "highlights issues found in different configurations. In the **Problems** panel,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "when you click an issue, you can see the details of the issue, suggested fixes,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "and the renderings that highlight the area of the issue."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![](https://developer.android.com/static/studio/images/design/compose-ui-check.png) **Figure 6.** UI check mode in action."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Fix with AI"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "For issues detected in UI Check mode, you can use the AI agent to propose and"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "apply code fixes. Click the **Fix with AI** button on an issue in the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Problems** panel. The agent analyzes the problem and your code to suggest"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "changes that resolve the accessibility or adaptive issue."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![](https://developer.android.com/static/studio/preview/features/images/ui-check-mode-single-fix.png) **Figure 7.** The agent fixes UI issues in UI Check mode."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
