  file_change {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///.agents/skills/appfunctions/references/kdoc-refinement-optimization.md"
    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    diff {
      unified_diff {
        lines {
          text: "Optimizes AppFunction KDoc for AI agents and Model Context Protocol."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Instructions"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Workflow: Agent-centric documentation"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "1. **Identify the core outcome** : Start the description with a strong imperative verb, for example, \"Search\", \"Create\", or \"Update\". Focus on the *user benefit*, not the code implementation."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "2. **Workflow dependencies** : Explicitly state if another function must be called first using the standard phrase: **Required workflow: Call \"Function"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   A\" first to \"Objective\"**."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "3. **Parameter documentation** :"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - For **functions** : Use specific `@param` tags. Isolate validation rules and default values here."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - For **serializables** : Use inline KDoc directly for each property declaration. KSP **won\'t** extract documentation from class-level tags."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "4. **Error surface mapping** : Rewrite `@throws` descriptions to provide useful recovery steps for the AI agent, for example \"If \"Error\", suggest the user check their internet connection.\""
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Workflow: Global app description for server instructions"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "When writing the `appfn:description` for `app_metadata.xml`, follow these"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "instructions:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "1. **Capture cross-function relationships**: Explain dependencies or sequences between tools, for example, \"Always call \'authenticate\' before fetching data.\"."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "2. **Document operational patterns**: Guide the LLM on token-conserving usage, for example, \"Use \'batch_update\' over multiple \'update\' calls.\""
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "3. **Specify constraints**: Define clear boundaries, for example, \"File operations limited to workspace\" or \"Rate limit: 10 requests per minute.\""
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "4. **Anti-patterns** :"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - Don\'t repeat individual function descriptions."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - Don\'t include marketing claims or subjective praise."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - Don\'t attempt to prompt model personality or conversation style."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Critical constraints"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Descriptive, not imperative"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Describe what the function *does* , not what the LLM *must* do. Avoid phrases"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "like \"You must call this...\" in favor of \"This function provides...\"."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### No \"fluff\""
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Remove conversational padding like \"This method is used to...\" or \"Helpful"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "for...\". Be concise and technical."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Inline KDoc for serializables"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Mandatory** : For `@AppFunctionSerializable` classes, documentation must be"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "inline for each property. KSP ignores class-level `@param` or `@property` tags"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "for these classes."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Examples"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Example: MCP refactoring"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Original**:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`/** This function helps you find people. */`"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Refined**:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "     /**"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "       * Search for message recipients by name or email."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "       * Required workflow: Call this before \"sendMessage\" to obtain valid recipient IDs."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "       * @param query Search string for name/email. If null, returns 3 most recent contacts."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "       * @return List of \"Recipient\" objects matching the query."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "       */"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Example: Global app description"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Refined**:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    This app provides functions for task management and team collaboration."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    Operational Patterns:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    - Always use \'searchUsers\' to resolve user handles to internal IDs before calling \'assignTask\'."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    - Prefer \'batchUpdateStatus\' when modifying more than three tasks simultaneously to reduce latency."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    Constraints:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    - Task titles are limited to 100 characters."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    - Attachment uploads are limited to 5 MB."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
