        lines {
          text: "# Basic DSL Recipe"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "This recipe shows a basic example of how to use the Navigation 3 API with two screens, using the `entryProvider` DSL and a persistent back stack."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## How it works"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "This example is similar to the basic recipe, but with a few key differences:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "1. **Persistent Back Stack** : It uses `rememberNavBackStack(RouteA)` to create and remember the back stack. This makes the back stack persistent across configuration changes (e.g., screen rotation). To use `rememberNavBackStack`, the navigation keys must be serializable, which is why `RouteA` and `RouteB` are annotated with `@Serializable` and implement the `NavKey` interface."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "2. **`entryProvider` DSL** : Instead of a `when` statement, this example uses the `entryProvider` DSL to define the content for each route. The `entry<RouteType>` function is used to associate a route type with its composable content."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The navigation logic remains the same: to navigate from `RouteA` to `RouteB`, we add a `RouteB` instance to the back stack."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[![](https://developer.android.com/static/images/picto-icons/code.svg) Explore View the full recipe on GitHub.](https://github.com/android/nav3-recipes/tree/main/app/src/main/java/com/example/nav3recipes/basicdsl)"
