    diff {
      unified_diff {
        lines {
          text: "# Conditional Navigation Recipe"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "This recipe demonstrates how to implement conditional navigation, where certain destinations are only accessible if a condition is met (in this case, if the user is logged in)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## How it works"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "This example has a `Profile` destination that requires the user to be logged in. If the user is not logged in and attempts to navigate to `Profile`, they are redirected to a `Login` screen. After a successful login, they are automatically navigated to the `Profile` screen."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### `AppBackStack`"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The core of this recipe is the custom `AppBackStack` class, which encapsulates the logic for conditional navigation."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **`RequiresLogin` interface** : A marker interface, `RequiresLogin`, is used to identify destinations that require the user to be logged in. The `Profile` destination implements this interface."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Redirecting to Login** : When the `add` function is called with a destination that implements `RequiresLogin` and the user is not logged in, `AppBackStack` stores the intended destination and adds the `Login` route to the back stack instead."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Handling Login** : When the `login` function is called, it sets the user\'s status to logged in. If there is a stored destination that the user was trying to access, it adds that destination to the back stack and removes the `Login` screen."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Handling Logout** : When the `logout` function is called, it sets the user\'s status to logged out and removes any destinations from the back stack that require the user to be logged in."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "This approach provides a clean way to handle conditional navigation by centralizing the logic in a custom back stack implementation."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[![](https://developer.android.com/static/images/picto-icons/code.svg) Explore View the full recipe on GitHub.](https://github.com/android/nav3-recipes/tree/main/app/src/main/java/com/example/nav3recipes/conditional)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
