        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Improve R8 optimization"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The performance benefits of R8 are directly correlated to how much of your"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "codebase R8 is able to optimize. To get the maximum benefits out of R8, follow"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "best practices:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Enable R8 in [full mode](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/full-mode)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Enable [obfuscation, optimization, and shrinking](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/adopt-optimizations-incrementally)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Enable resource shrinking and [optimized resource shrinking](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/enable-app-optimization#optimize-resource-shrinking)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- [Refine keep rules](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/keep-rules-best-practices) to allow maximum optimization of classes, fields and methods."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "To help you refine keep rules, use the [R8 Configuration Analyzer](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/r8-configuration-analyzer)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The R8 Configuration Analyzer lets you do the following:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Track and improve the overall R8 configuration quality by monitoring the metrics provided by the R8 Configuration Analyzer report."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Find the broadest keep rules - those which prevent the most optimization"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- and understand what optimization they prevent to refine them."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The R8 Configuration Analyzer is available in AGP version 9.3.0-alpha05 or from"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "R8 version 9.3.7-dev. For more information, see [Analyze R8 configuration](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/r8-configuration-analyzer)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Optimize resource shrinking for even smaller apps"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The 8.12.0 version of AGP introduces optimized resource shrinking, which aims to"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "integrate resource and code optimization to create even smaller and faster apps."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Before optimized resource shrinking, Android Asset Packaging Tool (AAPT2)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "generated keep rules that effectively treating resource shrinking separately"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "from code, often retaining inaccessible code or resources that referenced each"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "other."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "With optimized resource shrinking, resources are considered like a part of"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "program code, forming the reference graph. When a collection of code or"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "resources is not referenced, it is not protected by a keep rule, and can be"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "removed."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Enable optimized resource shrinking"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "To enable the new optimized resource shrinking pipeline for AGP 8.12 or 8.13,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "add the following to your project\'s `gradle.properties` file:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    android.r8.optimizedResourceShrinking=true"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "If you are using AGP 9.0.0 or a newer version, you don\'t need to set"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`android.r8.optimizedResourceShrinking=true`. Optimized resource shrinking is"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "automatically applied when `isShrinkResources = true` is enabled in your build"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "configuration."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Verify and configure R8 optimization settings"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "To enable R8 to use its [full optimization capabilities](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/full-mode), remove the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "following line from your project\'s `gradle.properties` file, if it exists:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    android.enableR8.fullMode=false"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Note that enabling app optimization makes stack traces difficult to understand,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "especially if R8 renames class or method names. To get stack traces that"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "correctly correspond to your source code, see [Recover the original stack"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "trace](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/test-and-troubleshoot-the-optimization#recover-original-stack-trace)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "If R8 is enabled, you should also [create Startup Profiles](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/baselineprofiles/dex-layout-optimizations) for even better"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "startup performance."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "If you enable app optimization and it causes errors, here are some strategies to"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "fix them:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- [Add keep rules](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/add-keep-rules) to keep some code untouched."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- [Adopt optimizations incrementally](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/adopt-optimizations-incrementally)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Update your code to [use libraries that are better suited for"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  optimization](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/choose-libraries-wisely)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> [!CAUTION]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Caution:** Tools that replace or modify R8\'s output can negatively impact runtime performance. R8 is careful about including and testing many optimizations at the code level, in [DEX layout](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/baselineprofiles/dex-layout-optimizations), and in correctly producing Baseline Profiles - other tools producing or modifying DEX files can break these optimizations, or otherwise regress performance."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "If you are interested in optimizing your build speed, see [Configure how R8"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "runs](https://developer.android.com/build/r8-execution-profiles) for information on how to configure R8 based on your environment."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## AGP and R8 version behavior changes"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The following table outlines the key features introduced in various versions of"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "the Android Gradle Plugin (AGP) and the R8 compiler."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| AGP version | Features introduced |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "|---|---|"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 9.3 | **Simplified DSL:** New \\`optimization {}\\` block enables requires less configuration- optimized resource shrinking is always enabled, default Android keep rules are opt-out. <br /> **\\`keepRules\\` source set:** If you use the new DSL, you must place your keep rules in the `src/<variant>/keepRules` source set, in files with the suffix `.keep`. The source sets are also compatible with the legacy DSL. <br /> **KMP (Kotlin MultiPlatform) consumer rules:** KMP no longer requires setting `publish = true`, and supports the `src/<variant>/keepRules` source set with the `.keep` extension. <br /> Note that the legacy DSL is still supported. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 9.1 | **Classes repackaged by default:** R8 repackages classes (moving them to the unnamed package, at the top level) to compact DEX further, eliminating the need to specify `-repackageclasses` option. For information about how this works and how to opt out, see [global options](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/global-options#global-options). |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 9.0 | **Optimized resource shrinking:** Enabled by default (controlled using `android.r8.optimizedResourceShrinking`). [Optimized resource shrinking](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/enable-app-optimization#optimize-resource-shrinking) helps integrate resource shrinking with the code optimization pipeline, leading to smaller, faster apps. By optimizing both code and resource references simultaneously, it identifies and removes resources referenced exclusively from unused code. This is a significant improvement over the previous separate optimization processes. This is especially useful for apps that share substantial resources and code across different form factor verticals, with measured improvements of over 50% in app size. The resulting size reduction leads to smaller downloads, faster installations, and a better user experience with faster startup, improved rendering, and fewer ANRs. **Library rule filtering:** Support for global options (for example, `-dontobfuscate`) in library consumer rules has been dropped, and apps will filter them out. For more information, see [Add global options](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/global-options). **Kotlin null checks:** Optimized by default (controlled using `-processkotlinnullchecks`). This version also introduced significant improvements in build speed. For more information, see [Global options for additional optimization](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/global-options#global-options). **Optimize specific packages:** You can use `packageScope` to optimize specific packages. This is in experimental support. For more information, see [Optimize specified packages with `packageScope`](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/optimize-specified-packages). **Optimized by default:** Support for `getDefaultProguardFile(\"proguard-android.txt\")` has been dropped, because it includes `-dontoptimize`, which should be avoided. Instead, use `\"proguard-android-optimize.txt\"`. If you need to globally disable optimization in your app, [add the flag manually to a proguard file](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/global-options#global-options-2). |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 8.12 | **Optimized resource shrinking:** Initial support added (controlled using `android.r8.optimizedResourceShrinking`). [Optimized resource shrinking](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/enable-app-optimization#optimize-resource-shrinking) helps integrate resource shrinking with the code optimization pipeline. You must manually enable it in this version of AGP. **Logcat retracing:** Support for automatic retracing in the Android Studio [Logcat window](https://developer.android.com/studio/debug/logcat). |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 8.6 | **Improved retracing:** Includes filename and line number retracing by default for all `minSdk` levels (previously required `minSdk` 26+ in version 8.2). Updating R8 helps ensure that stack traces from obfuscated builds are readily and clearly readable. This version improves how line numbers and source files are mapped, making it easier for tools like the Android Studio Logcat to automatically retrace crashes to the original source code. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 8.0 | **Full mode by default:** [R8 full mode](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/full-mode) provides significantly more powerful optimization. It is enabled by default. You can opt out using `android.enableR8.fullMode=false`. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 7.0 | **Full mode available:** Introduced as an opt-in feature using `android.enableR8.fullMode=true`. Full mode applies more powerful optimizations by making stricter assumptions about how your code uses reflection and other dynamic features. While it reduces app size and improves performance, it might require additional keep rules to prevent necessary code from being stripped. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Use R8 with other build systems"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "While AGP is the recommended and officially supported build system for Android"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "apps, you might use an alternative build system like [Bazel](https://bazel.build/). If"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "you\'re using Bazel, you can integrate R8 into your build pipeline to shrink,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "obfuscate, and optimize your app."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "For information about optimizing an Android app using Bazel, see Bazel\'s"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[`rules_android` documentation](https://github.com/bazelbuild/rules_android/tree/main/docs/r8-optimization.md). Note that Bazel isn\'t"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[officially supported](https://developer.android.com/build#other-build-systems) for Android app development."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_FILE_CHANGE
