        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Implement a fully custom design system"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "You may want to replace Material Theming with a fully custom design system."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Consider that `MaterialTheme` provides the following systems:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- `Colors`, `Typography`, and `Shapes`: Material Theming systems"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- `TextSelectionColors`: Colors used for text selection by `Text` and `TextField`"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- `Ripple` and `RippleTheme`: Material implementation of `Indication`"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "If you want to continue using Material components, you must replace some of"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "these systems in your custom themes or handle the systems in your"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "components to avoid unwanted behavior."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "However, design systems are not limited to the concepts Material relies on. You"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "can modify existing systems and introduce entirely new ones --- with new classes"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "and types --- to make other concepts compatible with themes."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "In the following code, we model a custom color system that includes gradients"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "(`List<Color>`), include a type system, introduce a new elevation system,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "and exclude other systems provided by `MaterialTheme`:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![Screenshot of a mobile app UI demonstrating a custom design system with elements using gradients for colors, custom typography, and elevation.](https://developer.android.com/static/develop/ui/compose/images/themes/custom-color-gradients.png)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
