steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_FILE_CHANGE
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1788915670
      nanos: 809183000
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
    completed_at {
      seconds: 1788915670
      nanos: 809183000
    }
  }
  file_change {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///.agents/skills/styles/references/android/develop/ui/compose/styles/styles-vs-modifiers.md"
    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    diff {
      unified_diff {
        lines {
          text: "Styles differ from modifiers by design. Styles don\'t replace modifiers; instead,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "the two systems coexist with different goals. Internally, a Style is a modifier."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "You can do everything Styles can do with modifiers, but not all functionality in"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "modifiers is available in Styles."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Important:**"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Choose Styles if:** You need to override a default of an existing component, perform high-performance animations, or define a theme-wide set of properties for a component."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Choose Modifiers if:** You need to add behavior (for example, clickable, gestures), define unique one-off layouts, or need additive properties."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The following is a comparison between Styles versus modifiers:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| Feature | Modifiers | Styles |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "|---|---|---|"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Primary Goal** | Define behaviors, semantics, and complex layouts. Modifiers manipulate individual elements on the fly for a particular composable and don\'t trickle down from the theme. | Define visual appearance, individual item sizing and themeable properties. Styles operate at a theme level and are over-writeable at a component level. They trickle down and apply styling across different composables. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Logic** | Additive - the modifiers combine together to form a new result. | Over-writable - the last property set in the Style wins. Styles act as a single layer of properties that override each other based on a defined precedence hierarchy. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Theming** | Challenging to lift into a theme, normally used individually. | By design, Styles are themeable (they can access `CompositionLocal`s) and can be defined once and used across components. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Performance** | Updates often require all three phases of Compose: composition, layout and draw. Achieving good animation performance of modifiers often requires writing lambda-based versions. | Skips composition phase, only active in layout and draw phase, reducing recompositions. Requires less object allocation. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Animations** | Requires using separate animation primitives like `animate*AsState` | Features built-in `animate { }` API that handles some animations for you. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Limitations of modifiers"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Modifiers have many benefits in the current Compose landscape. However, Styles"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "address some limitations of modifiers, which the following list describes:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Modifiers are typically created in the Composition phase. Updates can force a full rerun of Composition, Layout, and Draw, even for small visual changes like color, unless you create lambda-based modifiers."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Conditional modifiers require disruptive if-else logic within fluent chains. Animating them requires manual state boilerplate and lacks a high-performance \"auto-animate\" mechanism."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Modifiers stack rather than replace. You can\'t override a component\'s default border; you can only draw a second one on top."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Modifiers are difficult to abstract into global themes. Consequently, themes usually store raw values instead of reusable modifier configurations."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Limitations of Styles"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "While Styles can fill in some of the gaps that modifiers have, they also have"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "some limitations, which show how they cannot entirely replace modifiers:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Styles are specialized Modifiers. While a modifier can do anything a Style does, the reverse is not true. Consequently, Styles can supplement, but cannot replace, modifiers."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Styles are limited to visual configuration (backgrounds, padding, borders). They cannot handle behaviors like click logic, gesture detection, or accessibility semantics."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Resolving a Style into its final state is *more expensive than applying a"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  single modifier*. The system must generate a data structure containing all possible property values, and the lookup of inherited properties further complicates this."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## When to use Styles over modifiers"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "While the choice to use Styles is largely dependent on your app and use cases,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "the following guidance helps determine when to prefer a style over a modifier:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **To achieve theme-wide consistency:** Styles are designed to be \"lifted\" into a global theme. Instead of passing repetitive Modifiers to every component, you can define a single Style in your theme to create a unified look across the entire app."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **When performing frequent animations:** Styles evaluate during the Layout and Draw phases, allowing properties like color or scale to animate while bypassing the Composition phase entirely. This significantly reduces performance overhead. Use a Style instead of a modifier when doing visual property animations."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Overriding vs. stacking:** Use Styles when you need to replace a default property. Modifiers are additive (adding a border stacks a second one), whereas Styles use \"last-write-wins\" logic, making it easier to swap out backgrounds or padding without visual clutter."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Customizing Material components:** If a Material component provides a Style parameter, it is the suggested approach for customization. These styles allow you to access and modify specific properties within the composable\'s internal structure that might otherwise be inaccessible."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_FILE_CHANGE
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1788915670
      nanos: 809183000
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
    completed_at {
      seconds: 1788915670
      nanos: 809183000
    }
  }
  file_change {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///.agents/skills/styles/references/android/develop/ui/compose/styles/theming.md"
    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    diff {
      unified_diff {
        lines {
          text: "> [!NOTE]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Note:** Styles are `@Experimental` and likely to change in upcoming releases, with Material support for Styles added in future releases. If you have any feedback, [file Styles issues](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/new?component=612128)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "There are several ways you can build out your apps using Styles. What you choose"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "depends on where your app sits in relation to its adoption of Material Design:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "1. Fully custom design system, not using Material Design"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - **Recommendation**: Define component styles that consume values from the theme, and expose style parameters on design system components."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "2. Using Material Design"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - **Recommendation**: Await Material adoption to integrate with Styles. Use styles on your own components where possible."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Android skills"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[View on GitHub](https://github.com/android/skills/blob/main/jetpack-compose/theming/styles)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Use the Jetpack Compose Styles API"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Use the `styles` [Android skill](https://developer.android.com/tools/agents/android-skills) to create and customize components with the Styles API. To install the skill from the [Android CLI](https://developer.android.com/tools/agents/android-cli), run:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    android skills add styles"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "<br />"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## The Style layer"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "In the traditional Compose model, customization often relies heavily on"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "overriding global tokens (colors and typography) provided by `MaterialTheme`, or"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "wrapping and overriding properties of a design system composable where possible."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Sometimes, there are properties within the Material layer that are not exposed"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "through the subsystems or parameters, but are hardcoded defaults on the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "component itself."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "With the Styles API, there\'s a new layer of abstraction that\'s a bridge between"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "subsystems and components: **Styles**."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| Layer | Responsibility | Example |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "|---|---|---|"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Subsystem values** | Named values | `val Primary = Color(0xFF34A85E)` |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Atomic Styles** | Style that does exactly one property change | `val largeSizeAtomic = Style { size(100.dp, 40.dp) }` |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Component Styles** | Component-specific configurations | A Button with Primary background and 16dp padding. `val buttonStyle = Style { contentPadding(16.dp) shape(RoundedCornerShape(8.dp)) background(Color.Blue) }` |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Components** | The functional UI element that consumes a Style. | `Button(style = buttonStyle) { ... }` |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![Diagram showing Theming with Styles with the new layer introduction](https://developer.android.com/static/develop/ui/compose/styles/images/theming_styles_layer.png) **Figure 1.** An example of a component and how it accesses styles from a theme."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Atomic versus monolithic Styles"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "With the Styles API, you can break down a Style into separate atomic styles."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Instead of defining complex, component-specific styles like `baseButtonStyle`,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "you can also create small, single-purpose utility styles. These act as your"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "\"atoms\"."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "// Define single-purpose \"atomic\" styles"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "val paddingAtomic = Style {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    contentPadding(16.dp)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "val roundedCornerShapeAtomic = Style {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    shape(RoundedCornerShape(8.dp))"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "val primaryBackgroundAtomic = Style {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    background(Color.Blue)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "val largeSizeAtomic = Style {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    size(100.dp, 40.dp)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "val interactiveShadowAtomic = Style {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    hovered {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "        animate {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "            dropShadow("
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "                Shadow("
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "                    offset = DpOffset("
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "                        0.dp,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "                        0.dp"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "                    ),"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "                    radius = 2.dp,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "                    spread = 0.dp,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "                    color = Color.Blue,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "                )"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "            )"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "        }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "<br />"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "#### Composition using \"then\""
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The `then` operator in the Styles API lets you merge multiple `Style` objects."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "This lets you build a component using atomic utility classes."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Traditional (non-atomic)**:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "// One large monolithic style"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "val buttonStyle = Style {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    contentPadding(16.dp)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    shape(RoundedCornerShape(8.dp))"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    background(Color.Blue)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "<br />"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Atomic refactor**:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "// Combine atoms to create the final appearance"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "val buttonStyle = paddingAtomic then roundedCornerShapeAtomic then primaryBackgroundAtomic then interactiveShadowAtomic"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "<br />"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Adopt Styles in your design system"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Consider the following options when adopting Styles within your design system,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "depending on where in the spectrum your design system lies."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Custom design system with Styles"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "***Consider when**: You\'ve been handed an extensive brand guide that is not"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "based on Material Design, and you are not planning to use Material Design*."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "***Strategy**: Implement a fully custom design system, and expose styles as part"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "of the theme*."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "This option is the custom path if you don\'t use Material as your main design"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "system language. You bypass `MaterialTheme` entirely for visual definitions and"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "have created your [own custom theme already](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/designsystems/custom#implementing-fully-custom). You build a `CompanyTheme` that"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "acts as a container for your Styles."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **How it works** : Create a `CompanyTheme` object that holds `Style` objects for every component in your system. Your components (either wrappers around Material logic or custom `Box` or `Layout` implementations) consume these styles directly, and expose a `Style` parameter for consumers of your design system."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **The Style layer**: Styles are the primary definition of your design system. Tokens are named variables fed into these styles. This allows for deep customization, such as defining unique animations for state changes (for example, animating scale and color on press)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "If you are building out your own [custom theme](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/designsystems/custom) without using Material, and"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "want to adopt styles, add your list of styles to your Theme. This lets you"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "access your base styles from anywhere in your project."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "1. Create a `Styles` class that stores the various styles in your application"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   and create the defaults. For example, in the Jetsnack app - the class is"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   named `JetsnackStyles`:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   ```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   object JetsnackStyles{"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
