        lines {
          text: "[Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y9GWnwi9D0I)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "You can test your Compose app with well-established approaches and patterns."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Test in isolation"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[`ComposeTestRule`](https://developer.android.com/reference/kotlin/androidx/compose/ui/test/junit4/ComposeTestRule) lets you start an activity displaying any composable:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "your full application, a single screen, or a small element. It\'s also a good"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "practice to check that your composables are correctly encapsulated and they work"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "independently, allowing for easier and more focused UI testing."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "This doesn\'t mean you should *only* create unit UI tests. UI tests scoping"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "larger parts of your UI are also very important."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Access the activity and resources after setting your own content"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Oftentimes you need to set the content under test using"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`composeTestRule.setContent` and you also need to access activity resources, for"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "example to assert that a displayed text matches a string resource. However, you"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "can\'t call `setContent` on a rule created with `createAndroidComposeRule()` if"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "the activity already calls it."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "A common pattern to achieve this is to create an `AndroidComposeTestRule` using"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "an empty activity such as [`ComponentActivity`](https://developer.android.com/reference/androidx/activity/ComponentActivity)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    class MyComposeTest {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "        @get:Rule"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "        val composeTestRule = createAndroidComposeRule<ComponentActivity>()"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "        @Test"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "        fun myTest() {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "            // Start the app"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "            composeTestRule.setContent {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "                MyAppTheme {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "                    MainScreen(uiState = exampleUiState, /*...*/)"
