  file_change {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///.agents/skills/testing-setup/references/android/studio/preview/compose-screenshot-testing.md"
    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    diff {
      unified_diff {
        lines {
          text: "> [!WARNING]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Experimental:** Compose Preview Screenshot Testing is still in development. Its features and APIs are subject to change substantially during the alpha phase. Report any feedback and issues through the [issue tracker](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/new?component=192708&template=840533)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Screenshot testing is an effective way to verify how your UI looks to users."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The Compose Preview Screenshot Testing tool combines the simplicity and"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "features of [composable previews](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/tooling/previews) with the productivity"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "gains of running host-side screenshot tests. Compose Preview Screenshot Testing"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "is designed to be as straightforward to use as composable previews."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Android skills"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[View on GitHub](https://github.com/android/skills/blob/main/testing/testing-setup)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Create screenshot tests"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Use the `testing-setup` [Android skill](https://developer.android.com/tools/agents/android-skills) to develop a testing strategy and create screenshot tests. To install the skill from the [Android CLI](https://developer.android.com/tools/agents/android-cli), run:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    android skills add testing-setup"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "<br />"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "A screenshot test is an automated test that takes a screenshot of a piece of UI"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "and then compares it against a previously approved reference image. If the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "images don\'t match, the test fails and produces an HTML report to help you"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "compare and find the differences."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "With the Compose Preview Screenshot Testing tool, you can:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Use `@PreviewTest` to create screenshot tests for existing or new composable previews."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Generate reference images from those composable previews."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Generate an HTML report that identifies changes to those previews after you make code changes."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Use `@Preview` parameters, such as `uiMode` or `fontScale`, and multi-previews to help you scale your tests."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Modularize your tests with the new `screenshotTest` source set."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "![](https://developer.android.com/static/studio/images/compose-screenshot-testing.png) **Figure 1.** Example HTML report."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## IDE integration"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "While you can use the Compose Preview Screenshot Testing tool by running the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "underlying Gradle tasks (`updateScreenshotTest` and `validateScreenshotTest`)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "manually, Android Studio Otter 3 Feature Drop Canary 4 introduces a full IDE"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "integration. This lets you generate reference images, run tests, and analyze"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "validation failures entirely within the IDE. Here are some of the key features:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **In-editor gutter icons.** You can now run tests or update reference images directly from the source code. Green run icons appear in the gutter next to composables and classes annotated with `@PreviewTest`."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  - **Run screenshot tests.** Execute tests specifically for a single function or for an entire class."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  - **Add or update reference images.** Trigger the update flow specifically for the selected scope."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Interactive reference management.** Updating reference images is now safer and more granular."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  - **New reference image generation dialog.** Instead of running a bulk Gradle task, a new dialog lets you visualize and select exactly which previews to generate or update."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  - **Preview variations.** The dialog lists all preview variations (such as light theme or dark theme, or different devices) individually, allowing you to select or clear specific items before generating images."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Integrated test results and diff viewer.** View results without leaving the IDE."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  - **Unified run panel.** Screenshot test results appear in the standard **Run** tool window. Tests are grouped by class and function, with pass or fail status clearly marked."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  - **Visual diff tool.** When a test fails, the **Screenshot** tab lets you compare the *Reference* , *Actual* , and *Diff* images side-by-side."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  - **Detailed attributes.** An **Attributes** tab provides metadata on failed tests, including match percentage, image dimensions, and the specific preview configuration used (for example, `uiMode` or `fontScale`)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Flexible test scoping.** You can now execute screenshot tests with various scopes directly from the Project View. Right-click a module, directory, file, or class to run screenshot tests specifically for that selection."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Requirements"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "To use Compose Preview Screenshot Testing through the full IDE integration, your"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "project must meet the following requirements:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Android Studio Panda 1 Canary 4 or higher."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Android Gradle Plugin (AGP) version 9.0 or higher."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Compose Preview Screenshot Testing plugin version [0.0.1-alpha15](https://developer.android.com/studio/preview/compose-screenshot-testing-release-notes#alpha15) or higher."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Kotlin version 2.2.10 or higher."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- JDK version 17 or higher."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Compose enabled for your project. We recommend enabling Compose using the [Compose Compiler Gradle plugin](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/compiler)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "If you only want to use the underlying Gradle tasks without the IDE integration,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "the requirements are as follows:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Android Gradle Plugin (AGP) version 8.5.0 or higher."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Compose Preview Screenshot Testing plugin version [0.0.1-alpha15](https://developer.android.com/studio/preview/compose-screenshot-testing-release-notes#alpha15) or higher."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Kotlin version 1.9.20 or higher. We recommend using Kotlin 2.0 or higher so you can use the Compose Compiler Gradle plugin."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- JDK version 17 or higher."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Compose enabled for your project. We recommend enabling Compose using the [Compose Compiler Gradle plugin](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/compiler)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> [!NOTE]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Note:** If you can\'t use the Compose Compiler Gradle plugin, you can enable Compose by [declaring a dependency on the Compose Compiler directly](https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/compose-kotlin#kts). Make sure you use `kotlinCompilerExtensionVersion` version 1.5.4 or higher."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Setup"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Both the integrated tool and the underlying Gradle tasks rely on the Compose"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Preview Screenshot Testing plugin. To set up the plugin, follow these steps:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "1. Enable the experimental property in your project\'s `gradle.properties` file."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "       android.experimental.enableScreenshotTest=true"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "2. In the `android {}` block of your module-level `build.gradle.kts` file,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   enable the experimental flag to use the `screenshotTest` source set."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "       android {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "           experimentalProperties[\"android.experimental.enableScreenshotTest\"] = true"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "       }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "3. Add the `com.android.compose.screenshot` plugin, version `0.0.1-alpha15` to"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   your project."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   1. Add the plugin to your version catalogs file:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "          [versions]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "          agp = \"9.0.0-rc03\""
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "          kotlin = \"2.2.10\""
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "          screenshot = \"0.0.1-alpha15\""
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "          [plugins]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "          screenshot = { id = \"com.android.compose.screenshot\", version.ref = \"screenshot\"}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   2. In your module-level `build.gradle.kts` file, add the plugin in the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      `plugins {}` block:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "          plugins {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "              alias(libs.plugins.screenshot)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "          }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "4. Add the [`screenshot-validation-api`](https://maven.google.com/web/index.html?q=screenshot-validation-api#com.android.tools.screenshot:screenshot-validation-api)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   and [`ui-tooling`](https://maven.google.com/web/index.html?q=tooling#androidx.compose.ui:ui-tooling)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   dependencies."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "   1. Add them to your version catalogs:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "          [libraries]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "          screenshot-validation-api = { group = \"com.android.tools.screenshot\", name = \"screenshot-validation-api\", version.ref = \"screenshot\"}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
