    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    diff {
      unified_diff {
        lines {
          text: "One of the benefits of using dependency injection frameworks like Hilt is that"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "it makes testing your code easier."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Unit tests"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Hilt isn\'t necessary for unit tests, since when testing a class that uses"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "constructor injection, you don\'t need to use Hilt to instantiate that class."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Instead, you can directly call a class constructor by passing in fake or mock"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "dependencies, just as you would if the constructor weren\'t annotated:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "@ActivityScoped"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "class AnalyticsAdapter @Inject constructor("
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  private val service: AnalyticsService"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: ") { ... }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "class AnalyticsAdapterTest {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  @Test"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  fun `Happy path`() {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    // You don\'t need Hilt to create an instance of AnalyticsAdapter."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    // You can pass a fake or mock AnalyticsService."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    val adapter = AnalyticsAdapter(fakeAnalyticsService)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    assertEquals(...)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  }"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The same applies to ViewModel classes obtained by calling `hiltViewModel()` in"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "your composables. In unit tests, construct the ViewModel directly with fakes."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "For information on how state flows from a ViewModel into composables, see"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[State and Jetpack Compose](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/state) and [Where to hoist state](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/state-hoisting)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## End-to-end tests"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "For integration tests, Hilt injects dependencies as it would in your production"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "code. Testing with Hilt requires no maintenance because Hilt automatically"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "generates a new set of components for each test."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Adding testing dependencies"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "To use Hilt in your tests, include the `hilt-android-testing` dependency in your"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "project:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "dependencies {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    // For Robolectric tests."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    testImplementation(\"com.google.dagger:hilt-android-testing:2.57.1\")"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    kspTest(\"com.google.dagger:hilt-android-compiler:2.57.1\")"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    // For instrumented tests."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    androidTestImplementation(\"com.google.dagger:hilt-android-testing:2.57.1\")"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    kspAndroidTest(\"com.google.dagger:hilt-android-compiler:2.57.1\")"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    // Compose UI test rule."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    androidTestImplementation(\"androidx.compose.ui:ui-test-junit4\")"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    debugImplementation(\"androidx.compose.ui:ui-test-manifest\")"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> [!NOTE]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Note:** If you use [Jetpack integrations](https://developer.android.com/training/dependency-injection/hilt-jetpack) (like `hilt-navigation-compose` to obtain a ViewModel through `hiltViewModel()`), you must also add their annotation processors to your test dependencies."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### UI test setup"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "You must annotate any UI test that uses Hilt with `@HiltAndroidTest`. This"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "annotation is responsible for generating the Hilt components for each test."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Also, you need to add the `HiltAndroidRule` to the test class. It manages the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "components\' state and is used to perform injection on your test:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "@HiltAndroidTest"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "class SettingsScreenTest {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    @get:Rule(order = 0)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    val hiltRule = HiltAndroidRule(this)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    @get:Rule(order = 1)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    val composeRule = createAndroidComposeRule<HiltTestActivity>()"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "    // Compose UI tests here."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> [!NOTE]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Note:** If you have other rules in your test, see [Multiple TestRule objects in"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> your instrumented test](https://developer.android.com/training/dependency-injection/hilt-testing#multiple-testrules)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Next, your test needs to know about the `Application` class that Hilt"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "automatically generates for you."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "To let Hilt inject dependencies, you must create an empty activity named"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`HiltTestActivity` in your `androidTest` source set and annotate it with"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`@AndroidEntryPoint`. `createAndroidComposeRule` then uses this activity as the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "host for your composable content."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "#### Test application"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "You must execute instrumented tests that use Hilt in an `Application` object"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "that supports Hilt. The library provides `HiltTestApplication` for use in tests."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "If your tests need a different base application, see [Custom application for"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "tests](https://developer.android.com/training/dependency-injection/hilt-testing#custom-application)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "You must set your test application to run in your [instrumented"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "tests](https://developer.android.com/training/testing/ui-testing) or [Robolectric"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "tests](http://robolectric.org/). The following instructions aren\'t"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "specific to Hilt, but are general guidelines on how to specify a custom"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "application to run in tests."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "##### Set the test application in instrumented tests"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "To use the Hilt test application in [instrumented"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "tests](https://developer.android.com/training/testing/ui-testing), you need to configure a new test runner."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "This makes Hilt work for all of the instrumented tests in your project. Perform"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "the following steps:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "1. Create a custom class that extends [`AndroidJUnitRunner`](https://developer.android.com/reference/kotlin/androidx/test/runner/AndroidJUnitRunner) in the `androidTest` folder."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "2. Override the `newApplication` function and pass in the name of the generated Hilt test application."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
