        lines {
          text: "#### Binding new values"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Use the `@BindValue` annotation to easily bind fields in your test into the Hilt"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "dependency graph. Annotate a field with `@BindValue` and it will be bound under"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "the declared field type with any qualifiers that are present for that field."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "In the `AnalyticsService` example, you can replace `AnalyticsService` with a"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "fake by using `@BindValue`:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "@UninstallModules(AnalyticsModule::class)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "@HiltAndroidTest"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "class SettingsScreenTest {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  @BindValue @JvmField"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  val analyticsService: AnalyticsService = FakeAnalyticsService()"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  ..."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "This simplifies both replacing a binding and referencing a binding in your test"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "by allowing you to do both at the same time."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`@BindValue` works with qualifiers and other testing annotations. For example,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "if you use testing libraries such as"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[Mockito](https://site.mockito.org/), you could use it in a"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Robolectric test as follows:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "..."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "class SettingsScreenTest {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  ..."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  @BindValue @ExampleQualifier @Mock"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  lateinit var qualifiedVariable: ExampleCustomType"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  // Robolectric tests here"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "If you need to add a [multibinding](https://dagger.dev/dev-guide/multibindings),"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "you can use the `@BindValueIntoSet` and `@BindValueIntoMap` annotations in place"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "of `@BindValue`. `@BindValueIntoMap` requires you to also annotate the field"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "with a map key annotation."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Special cases"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Hilt also provides features to support nonstandard use cases."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Custom application for tests"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "If you cannot use `HiltTestApplication` because your test application needs to"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "extend another application, annotate a new class or interface with"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`@CustomTestApplication`, passing in the value of the base class you want the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "generated Hilt application to extend."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`@CustomTestApplication` will generate an `Application` class ready for testing"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "with Hilt that extends the application you passed as a parameter."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "@CustomTestApplication(BaseApplication::class)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "interface HiltTestApplication"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "In the example, Hilt generates an `Application` named"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`HiltTestApplication_Application` that extends the `BaseApplication` class. In"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "general, the name of the generated application is the name of the annotated"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "class appended with `_Application`. You must set the generated Hilt test"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "application to run in your [instrumented tests](https://developer.android.com/training/testing/ui-testing) or"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[Robolectric tests](http://robolectric.org/) as described in [Test"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "application](https://developer.android.com/training/dependency-injection/hilt-testing#test-application)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> [!NOTE]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "> **Note:** Because `HiltTestApplication_Application` is code that Hilt generates at runtime, the IDE might highlight it in red until you run your tests."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Multiple TestRule objects in your instrumented test"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Compose UI tests already combine `HiltAndroidRule` with a Compose test rule"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "such as `createAndroidComposeRule`. If you have additional `TestRule` objects,"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "make sure `HiltAndroidRule` runs first. Declare the execution order with the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`order` attribute on `@Rule`:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "@HiltAndroidTest"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "class SettingsScreenTest {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  @get:Rule(order = 0)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  var hiltRule = HiltAndroidRule(this)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  @get:Rule(order = 1)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  val composeRule = createAndroidComposeRule<HiltTestActivity>()"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  @get:Rule(order = 2)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  val otherRule = SomeOtherRule()"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  // UI tests here."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Alternatively, you can wrap the rules with `RuleChain`, placing"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "`HiltAndroidRule` as the outer rule."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```kotlin"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "@HiltAndroidTest"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "class SettingsScreenTest {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  @get:Rule"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  var rule = RuleChain.outerRule(HiltAndroidRule(this))."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "        around(SettingsScreenTestRule(...))"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "  // UI tests here."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "}"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Use an entry point before the singleton component is available"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "The `@EarlyEntryPoint` annotation provides an escape hatch when a Hilt entry"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "point needs to be created before the singleton component is available in a"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "Hilt test."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "More information about `@EarlyEntryPoint` in the"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "[Hilt documentation](https://dagger.dev/hilt/early-entry-point)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "## Additional resources"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "To learn more about testing, see the following additional resources:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Documentation"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- [Test your Compose layout](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/testing)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- [Testing cheatsheet](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/testing/testing-cheatsheet)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "### Views content"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "- [Hilt testing guide (Views)](https://developer.android.com/topic/architecture/views/dependency-injection/hilt-testing-views)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
